 "notes": "Rössen culture (4,600-4,300 BC, Central Europe), typed culture like the Linear Pottery and Lengyel dossiers; Cliopatria has no row. Three pages opened.\n\nTo settle: (1) The LBK keyframe (-4800..-4500) overlaps this shape in -4600..-4500 across the Rhine, Bavaria, Hesse and northern Switzerland; a ruling or a trimmed LBK keyframe is needed (the linear-pottery-culture dossier dissolves to 'nobody' at -4500 and records no loss to the Rössen). (2) The Hinkelstein, Großgartach and Planig-Friedberg complexes (between LBK and Rössen in the west) and the post-Rössen groups (Bischheim, Gatersleben), Lengyel (south), Pfyn (northern Switzerland) and the Funnelbeaker Baalberge (north) have no dossier and no dates on the page; at -4300 the land outside the Michelsberg shape is recorded as nobody's. (3) The Austrian part is unplaced ('a small part of Austria'), so Austria is not drawn. (4) The Austrian, Swiss and French parts are the researcher's reading as admin units; Bavaria and Saxony are included under 'Germany except north' and the page does not list the 11 states. Southern Lower Saxony is a 100 km disc at Hildesheim intersected with Lower Saxony. (5) The infobox range line 'Northern and Central Hesse, Westphalia, South Lower Saxony, West Thuringia' duplicates the Wartberg culture's infobox and was not used as a core. (6) Gazetteer names used (Lorraine, Alsace, Champagne, Hildesheim and the admin1 units) all resolve."
